# tools/m/mantra_document_roundtrip_witness.rish -- does the store return the bytes it was handed?
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES. Mantra is a version store, so the first thing it owes a
# caller is the document it was given. `cmd_add` in `mantra/src/main.rye` stores
# what `split_lines` in `mantra/src/diff.rye` hands it and nothing beside it: a
# weave and a commit, never the file's own bytes. So whatever the split cannot
# tell apart, the store cannot tell apart either.
#
# THE DEFECT, and the repair that closed it. Until `20260917` the split broke its
# loop at the empty token a text ending in `\n` produces, so `x\ny` and `x\ny\n`
# split to one list of two lines. Measured on metal `20260910.043900`: two pens,
# two files differing by exactly the final newline, one `mantra add` each -- both
# answered `HEAD -> 441c3c6fa8b8` and both weaves carried the digest
# `7695a361c00e...`. A content-addressed store gave one address to two contents,
# and it was never only a display fault: `mantra status` called the changed file
# **clean** and `mantra add` answered `unchanged -- nothing to weave`, in both
# directions, so the store declined the change even when asked for it directly.
#
# WHY IT TOOK THREE ROUNDS TO CLOSE. REDS %689 booked the loss and named three
# doors, each costing something a lap may not spend alone. Keaton ruled door 2 on
# `20260916.000449` -- a weave records the terminator as HISTORY, so the trailing
# token becomes a LINE the weave keeps, inserted when a newline is appended and
# deleted when one is removed. That build was proven and then WITHDRAWN, because
# keeping the token turns every APPEND into a MIDDLE INSERT and a middle insert
# was %680's own defect. %680 closed on `20260916.061223`: `Diff` carries `after`
# and `Weave.apply` inherits the anchor's run and order key. The repair landed on
# `20260917` on that footing.
#
# WHAT IS GATED, AND THE ONE READING STILL REPORTED. Seven readings naming the
# loss were REPORTED while the repair wanted a ruling, since a gate that reds on
# what no lap may repair is a gate somebody turns off -- the same placement
# `.claude/rules/derived-spine.md` takes for a published double. The ruling came
# and the repair landed, so all seven are walls now. `raw_bytes_in_store` stays
# REPORTED: door 3 -- write the file's own bytes as a blob and name it in the
# commit -- was never taken, and it widens the `file` row when it is.
#
# AND A SECOND DEFECT IS REPORTED HERE NOW, for the same reason the seven were.
# REDS %807: a line inserted at the HEAD of a stored document leaves it. `diff`
# computes each insert's anchor as the last kept line BEFORE the gap, and the gap
# opening a document has no line before it, so `apply` falls back to the weave's
# own counter and the new line sorts past every line the weave holds. `mantra
# status` then answers `1 added, 1 removed` with the SAME text on both sides -- a
# move -- on a file nothing has touched. The unit level has held this since
# `20260916` as `prove_head_insert_lands_last` in
# `mantra/src/weave_apply_witness.rye`, and no reading pressed the CLI, so the
# user-visible half stood under no guard at all. That is the row's own teaching:
# a limit stated only in the code it limits is a limit no lap is asked to close.
# The three doors -- a `before` anchor with nowhere to put its key, renumbering
# every `ord` and breaking merge, or reserving a floor that buys one head insert
# per weave -- are a ruling about how places are ASSIGNED, so these readings name
# the loss and gate nothing.
#
# THE PRICE, NAMED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. A three-line terminated file reports FOUR
# lines now, and every weave already on disk drifts by one on its next add. That
# cost was written into door 2 before it was chosen, and the control measures it
# on two built binaries rather than asserting it.
#
# BOTH DIRECTIONS. Three control legs break the CLI -- one that never weaves, one
# whose status never reads clean, and one that restores the elder split rule and
# watches all four walls fall at once. A guard that only ever says `no` cannot be
# told from a broken binary, which is why `lawful_change_seen` presses from the
# passing side in the scan itself.
#
# Siblings: the record the CLI writes at tools/m/mantra_cli_record_witness.rish,
# the reader's ceiling at tools/m/mantra_record_ceiling_witness.rish, the
# idempotent add at tools/m/mantra_idempotent_add_witness.rish.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/m/mantra_document_roundtrip_witness.rish

say "mantra-document-roundtrip: Language EN -- a store owes back the document it was handed."
say "mantra-document-roundtrip: Style Gauge, Meter -- every claim is an answer a built CLI gave in a pen."
say "mantra-document-roundtrip: Lens TAME -- safety first, and a store that loses a byte is a safety fault."

say "mantra-document-roundtrip: the split rule this guard reads is still the one on disk..."
let seat = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'if (text.len == 0) return &.{};' mantra/src/diff.rye && ! grep -q 'if (line.len == 0 and it.rest().len == 0) break;' mantra/src/diff.rye"]
assert seat.ok else "mantra-document-roundtrip: split_lines stopped keeping the terminator, or stopped answering zero for empty text -- either way this header and every gate below are reading a module that has moved (REDS %689)"

say "mantra-document-roundtrip: cmd_add still stores a weave and a commit rather than the file's bytes..."
let stored = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'const weave_blob  = try serialize_weave' mantra/src/main.rye"]
assert stored.ok else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the add path changed shape, so what this guard says about where the bytes go needs re-reading"

say "mantra-document-roundtrip: building the tree's own CLI and handing it two documents one byte apart..."
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/m/mantra_document_roundtrip_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the scan must complete"
assert scan.out contains "built=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the CLI did not compile, so every reading below is a reading of nothing"
assert scan.out contains "lawful_change_seen=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: an ordinary edit stopped being woven, so the readings that say no below say nothing"
assert scan.out contains "lawful_status_seen=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: status stopped reporting an ordinary edit, and the same objection applies"
assert scan.out contains "terminated_roundtrip=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: a file ending in a newline no longer reads back clean against its own weave"
assert scan.out contains "bare_roundtrip=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: a file ending without a newline no longer reads back clean against its own weave"
# THE SEVEN READINGS THAT WERE REPORTED UNTIL `20260917`, walled now that the
# repair has landed. Each names one face of REDS %689: two documents one byte
# apart earning one address, and a store that declined the change even when
# asked for it directly.
assert scan.out contains "weave_digest_shared=no" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: two documents one byte apart earn one weave name again -- the defect REDS %689 booked, returned"
assert scan.out contains "commit_digest_shared=no" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: and one commit name, so the whole store cannot tell the two apart"
assert scan.out contains "status_sees_newline_added=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: status calls a file clean after a newline was appended to it"
assert scan.out contains "add_sees_newline_added=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: add declines to weave an appended newline, so the store refuses the change when asked for it directly"
assert scan.out contains "status_sees_newline_removed=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: status calls a file clean after its final newline was taken away"
assert scan.out contains "add_sees_newline_removed=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: add declines to weave a removed newline -- the same loss from the other side"
# THE HEAD INSERT (REDS %807, OPEN). `head_insert_woven` is GATED from the
# passing side: `add` does weave a line inserted at the head, so a `no` here
# means the store stopped seeing the edit and the two readings after it say
# nothing. The two themselves are REPORTED, because the repair is a choice among
# three doors and none is a lap's to take alone -- the same placement the seven
# readings above held while %689 waited on Keaton's word. They are asserted
# PRESENT rather than valued, so a reading that stops being printed is heard the
# lap it goes quiet; a reported reading nobody quotes is the one that can vanish
# without reddening anything.
assert scan.out contains "head_insert_woven=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: add stopped weaving a line inserted at the head of a document, so the two readings below are readings of nothing"
assert scan.out contains "head_insert_roundtrip=" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the head-insert roundtrip reading stopped being printed, and a reported reading nobody quotes can go quiet without reddening anything"
assert scan.out contains "head_insert_reports_move=" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the head-insert move signature stopped being printed -- the same objection"
assert scan.out contains "terminator_invisible=no" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the terminator is invisible to the store again, which is REDS %689 in one word"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the scan reached its own red"

say "mantra-document-roundtrip: breaking the CLI twice, and pricing door 1 once, in a pen..."
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/m/mantra_document_roundtrip_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the control must complete -- a witness nobody has watched fail is a witness nobody has tested"
assert control.out contains "fail=0" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: a control leg failed, and control_verdict alone says only that the pen reached its last line"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the control must reach its own verdict"
assert control.out contains "pen_built=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the pen copy did not build, so every mutation below fails for a reason the pen invented"
assert control.out contains "pen_baseline_ok=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the unmutated pen must read exactly as the tree does"
assert control.out contains "frozen_add_bites=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: a CLI that never weaves must red the scan, or the gate is not reading the add path"
assert control.out contains "frozen_named=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: that break must be named by lawful_change_seen rather than by some other reading"
assert control.out contains "dirty_status_bites=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: a CLI whose status never reads clean must red the scan, or the roundtrip readings are constants"
assert control.out contains "elder_drop_planted=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the elder-drop plant named a line the module no longer has, so the pen ran the UNMUTATED module and every reading below is a reading of a healthy tree"
assert control.out contains "elder_drop_builds=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the elder-drop mutation did not compile, so nothing below it was measured"
assert control.out contains "elder_drop_shares_weave=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: restoring the elder drop must put the two documents back on one weave name, or that wall is holding for a reason this guard has not found"
assert control.out contains "elder_drop_shares_commit=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: and back on one commit name"
assert control.out contains "elder_drop_blind_to_add=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: and add must go blind to an appended newline again"
assert control.out contains "elder_drop_hides_seam=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: and the seam reading must go invisible again"
assert control.out contains "elder_drop_reds_scan=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the scan must reach red under the elder drop -- a wall proven only by a healthy tree cannot be told from a constant"
assert control.out contains "elder_drop_keeps_lawful=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: an ordinary edit must still be woven under the elder drop, or the pen broke something wider than the split rule"
assert control.out contains "clean_status_planted=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the always-clean plant named a line the CLI no longer has, so that pen ran the UNMUTATED module and the two flips below are readings of a healthy tree"
assert control.out contains "clean_status_builds=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the always-clean mutation did not compile, so nothing under it was measured"
assert control.out contains "clean_status_flips_roundtrip=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: head_insert_roundtrip could not be made to answer yes, so it is a constant rather than a reading"
assert control.out contains "clean_status_flips_move=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: head_insert_reports_move could not be made to answer no -- the same objection from the other side"
assert control.out contains "clean_status_bites=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: a status calling every file clean must red the gate by name, or that pen is broken in a way no reading names"
assert control.out contains "clean_status_keeps_woven=yes" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the head insert stopped being woven under a plant that only touched reporting, so the two flips above moved for a reason this leg has not found"
assert control.out contains "head_insert_position=4" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: a line inserted at the head of a three-line document lands somewhere other than last -- which is either REDS %807 repaired or the pen measuring something else, and both want a reading rather than a silent pass"
assert control.out contains "elder_drop_line_count=3" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the elder drop reports three lines for a three-line terminated file; a different number means the plant did something else"
assert control.out contains "tree_line_count=4" else "mantra-document-roundtrip: the tree reports four -- three lines a hand wrote and the terminator -- and that one line is the whole price of the repair"

say "GREEN: twelve roundtrip readings gated, the terminator a line of the history, three still reported -- door 3 and the two naming REDS %807 -- nineteen control legs, four breaks caught, the closed defect shown reappearing whole and the open one measured landing last."
